We can help more if you're more specific... Maybe you're delaying when 
you don't need to.

A relatively safe Ascension Kit is one which provides the following:
All the intrinsics acquired by eating
200+ HP
-30 AC+
Magic Resistance
Reflection
A way to levitate or fly
teleportation wands to clear paths
fire and lightning wands to burn E
full healing and holy water/remove curse scrolls in a non BOH bag
A way to find the portals (the AoY works in a pinch, but it means 
delays, which means more fighting)

With somewhat careful play, that's all you need.  Free Action is good, 
hasted jumping is killer.

That said, it sounds more like you reach a comfort zone in the game, 
then decide to quit (do you mean hibernate the character, or #quit?) due 
to boredom.  There's nothing exciting like descending *past* where you'd 
normally feel safe in search of loot!

For the *really* reckless approach, Dive For Victory.  Get a digging 
implement (pickaxe or mattock), save /WoDiggings for quick escapes.
Get a musical instrument other than a whistle.  Both pickaxes and other 
tools come more frequently in the mines.  Now comes the scary part.
On every level, dig down, till you hit the Castle.  When you get there, 
if a purple L is there, stand on an engraved E-word till he's dead or 
escapes.  Play mastermind for the drawbridge till all the non-phasing 
critters are toast, then run yer ass for the /WoW.  With a /WoW, wish 
for 2 blessed scrolls of charging (if you don't have them yet), then 
wish up as much of the essential ascension kit as you can.  Don't forget 
reflection for the trip up while your exploring, as you left Medusa in 
the dust a little while back, and you'll come upon her on the way up.

To do this, with reasonable success rates (well, ok, it's a reckless 
scheme anyway, but *less* reckless) you need:
to clear out the mines down to at least minetown for the tool shop.  If 
no musical instruments there, keep clearing, but be careful of 
poly-traps once you go lower than Dlvl 7.
clear out Sokoban for the wands and scrolls of earth and prize at end.
A potion of object detection.
A way to detect monsters.  (even a non-cursed potion will do, just to 
check for purple L's, but intrinsic telepathy and blindfold or towel is 
best)

With no musical instruments, it becomes more risky, as you need a way to 
kill the door at range, then a way to cross the moat.  A carefully 
placed scroll of earth can do this.  'E-word' and just take the monsters 
  one at a time.  Be prepared to fight soldiers, if that's the case.

That's just one strategy, and not the most careful, but it has a higher 
win rate than #quitting!  ;-)  Have patience, play careful.  Remember 
that Nethack is turn based, not real time.

